{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.TannakaDual","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.TannakaDual","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.NaturalTransformation","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Endomorphism"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.groupTannakaDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.groupTannakaDual","kind":"instance","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/tannaka-dual.lean#L35-L42","doc":"The Tannaka dual is a group: monoidal natural automorphisms of `τ` compose\nand invert. (The instance is inherited from `Aut`; stated explicitly as the\ngauge-group content.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaDual","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/tannaka-dual.lean#L27-L33","doc":"**Tannaka dual / emergent gauge group** `G = Aut⊗(τ)` of a fibre functor\n`τ`. Automorphisms are taken in the category of monoidal functors — whose\nmorphisms are monoidal natural transformations — so `Aut τ` is precisely\nthe group of *tensor*-natural automorphisms. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:tannaka-dual","label":"def:tannaka-dual","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/tannaka-dual.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}